# What is deliberately kept out of the repository, and why.
# See README.md section 7 for how to obtain the two large datasets.

# Every dataset is committed, including pumsb_negative.txt (27 MB) and accidents_negative.txt
# (71 MB), because the supervisor asked for the input data to be in the repository. Both are
# under GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit, so Git LFS is not needed.

# --- Published papers: redistributing the publisher PDF is not ours to do ---
1-s2.0-S0020025521012457-main.pdf
1-s2.0-S0952197623003664-main.pdf
Mining periodic high-utility itemsets with both positive and negative utilities.pdf

# --- Experiment results. The 172 pattern files total 181 MB but hold only 24 distinct
#     contents: the repeated E8 runs write byte-identical output, which is precisely what E8
#     measured, and the published build writes empty files. One representative of each distinct
#     content is committed below, a run of the patched build ("_f_") whenever the group has one;
#     output/MANIFEST_output.csv names all 172 originals with their size, MD5 and
#     representative, so nothing is lost. Regenerate both the manifest and this list with
#     `py -I tools/manifest_output.py`. ---
output/*.txt
!output/ablation_E0.txt
!output/accidents_f_13000000.txt
!output/accidents_f_19000000_minavg1.txt
!output/chess_d7_150000.txt
!output/chess_f_150000.txt
!output/chess_f_80000.txt
!output/chess_lo_1.txt
!output/chess_lo_100.txt
!output/chess_lo_1000.txt
!output/docExample_PHMN.txt
!output/e8_a_mushroom_100000_ma10_r1.txt
!output/e8_a_mushroom_100000_ma5_r1.txt
!output/mushroom_d7_100000_p1-3000-1-2000.txt
!output/mushroom_dt_100000_p1-3000-1-2000.txt
!output/mushroom_f_100000_p1-3000-1-2000.txt
!output/pumsb_dt_5000000.txt
!output/pumsb_dt_5200000.txt
!output/pumsb_dt_5400000.txt
!output/pumsb_dt_5600000.txt
!output/pumsb_f_5400000.txt
!output/pumsb_f_5600000.txt
!output/pumsb_f_5800000.txt
!output/strategy4_counterexample_patched.txt
!output/strategy4_counterexample_stock.txt
